nd":"axiom","plain":"Formal clause: data labels propagate along flows; untrusted labels reach privileged sinks only through declared transforms satisfying sink policy.","principles":["P-9","P-14"],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"A kitchen tracks one tag per ingredient; tracing how information flows and combines needs more than that, which the picture does not cover.","maps":[{"analogy":"the allergen tag that travels with the ingredient","doctrine":"the origin label and trust limit carried with the value"},{"analogy":"the documented step that removes or contains the allergen before serving","doctrine":"the declared cleaning step before a sensitive output"}],"text":"Allergen information has to follow an ingredient all the way through the kitchen. A clean-looking label on the final plate counts for nothing if nobody tracked the nuts."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A public page prints a value copied from private files because the final copy step looked clean, with no record of where the value came from.","does_not_prove":"Only the flows that are actually traced are checked; the registry records that tracing every flow through the whole system is unfinished.","enforced_in_component_ids":["indirect_prompt_injection_information_flow_policy_replay","macro_projection_import_protocol"],"example":{"component_ids":["indirect_prompt_injection_information_flow_policy_replay"],"text":"The prompt-injection replay carries the information-flow policy along with the data, so untrusted instructions that arrive at a tool call are stopped there instead of being trusted because they reached a trusted endpoint."},"governs":"How material and its trust label move between steps.","plain":"A record of where a value came from, and how far it may travel, must follow it everywhere. Untrusted material can reach a sensitive place only after a stated cleaning step.","potential_misread":"That a clean label at the end means the path was clean, when only a label carried all the way, with a declared cleaning step, counts.","refuses":"An output claiming a clean label that was never carried there from the source.","requires":"An origin label and a limit on what it supports, carried with the value, and a declared cleaning step before untrusted material reaches a sensitive output.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"Private, outside or unverified input cannot reach a public or privileged output just because the final step looked clean."},"rests_on":[],"source_ref":"AXIOMS.md::AX-8","statement":"Formal clause: data labels propagate along flows; untrusted labels reach\nprivileged sinks only through declared transforms satisfying sink policy.\n\nLineage: Denning information-flow lattice, Biba integrity, taint tracking,\nnon-interference.\n\nRoute: recorded as partially witnessed by\n`indirect_prompt_injection_information_flow_policy_replay`, the private-state\nand secret-exclusion scans, the release export gates, and the engine-room paper\nmodules on egress and public projection. Negative cases cover private-state\nclasses and leaks into public pages. One layer-debt receipt is open: labels are\nnot yet tracked across a general graph of flows.\n\nAnti-axiom: a label asserted at the end of a pipeline replaces tracking where\nthe data came from.","statement_sha256":"a71104a269d75181675473d412b9f25f747f1d62ecdbf3da66e610fc5af9bcc3","title":"Provenance propagation and non-interference","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}